given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rapid and direct detection of <italic>Clostridium chauvoei </italic>by PCR of the 16S-23S rDNA spacer region and partial 23S rDNA sequences</article-title><source>J Vet Med Sci</source><year>2000</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>1275</fpage><lpage>1281</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11193343</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1292/jvms.62.1275</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sasaki</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kojima</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Aoki</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ogikubo</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Takikawa</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Tamur</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phylogenetic analysis and PCR detection of <italic>Clostridium chauvoei</italic>, <italic>Clostridium haemolyticum</italic>, <italic>Clostridium novyi </italic>types A and B, and <italic>Clostridium septicum </italic>based on the flagelin gene</article-title><source>Vet Microbiology</source><year>2002</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>257</fpage><lpage>267</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0378-1135(02)00002-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benson</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Karsch-Mizrachi</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Lipman</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ostell</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Wheeler</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>GenBank</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>2007</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>D21</fpage><lpage>D25</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17202161</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/nar/gkl986</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>B&#x000e5;verud</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Gustafsson</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Franklin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Aspan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gunnarsson</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>Clostridium difficile</italic>: prevalence in horses, in environment and antimicrobial susceptibility</article-title><source>Equine Vet J</source><year>2003</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>465</fpage><lpage>471</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12875324</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2746/042516403775600505</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Uzal</surname><given-names>FA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hugenholtz</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Blackall</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Petray</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Moss</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Assis</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Fernandez Miyakawa</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Carloni</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>PCR detection of <italic>Clostridium chauvoei </italic>in pure cultures and in formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded tissues</article-title><source>Vet Microbiol</source><year>2003</year><volume>91</volume><fpage>239</fpage><lpage>248</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12458172</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0378-1135(02)00291-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kuhnert</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Krampe</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Capaul</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Frey</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicolet</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of <italic>Clostridium chauvoei </italic>in cultures and clinical material from blackleg using PCR</article-title><source>Vet Microbiol</source><year>1997</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>291</fpage><lpage>298</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9355263</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0378-1135(97)00129-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sasaki</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamamoto</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Amimot</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kojima</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ogikubo</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Norimatsu</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ogata</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Tamura</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Amplification of the 16S-23S rDNA spacer region for rapid detection of <italic>Clostridium chauvoei </italic>and <italic>Clostridium septicum</italic></article-title><source>Res Vet Sci</source><year>2001</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>229</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11798300</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1053/rvsc.2001.0495</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Takeuchi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hashizume</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Kinoshita</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaidoh</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tamura</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Detection of <italic>Clostridium septicum </italic>hemolysin gene by polymerase chain reaction</article-title><source>J Vet Med Sci</source><year>1997</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>853</fpage><lpage>855</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9342717</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1292/jvms.59.853</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rossen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>N&#x000f8;rskov</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Holmstr&#x000f8;m</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Rasmussen</surname><given-names>OF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inhibition of PCR by components of blood samples, microbial diagnostic assays and DNA-extraction solutions</article-title><source>Int J Food Microbiol</source><year>1992</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1476866</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0168-1605(92)90017-W</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Munang'andu</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Muyoyeta</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mweene</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Kida</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bovine clostridial infections in Zambia</article-title><source>Jpn J Vet Res</source><year>1996</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>175</fpage><lpage>178</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8997878</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burtscher</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Wuertz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of the use of PCR and reverse transcriptase PCR for detection of pathogenic bacteria in biosolids from anaerobic digestor and aerobic composters</article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><year>2003</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>4618</fpage><lpage>4627</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12902250</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/AEM.69.8.4618-4627.2003</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>